@startuml
title One sampling window: what reaches policy, and what stays diagnostics

skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam roundCorner 10
skinparam defaultFontName Helvetica
skinparam defaultFontColor #111827
skinparam ArrowColor #4B5563
skinparam ArrowFontColor #374151
skinparam activity {
  BorderColor #4B5563
  FontColor #111827
  BackgroundColor #F8FAFC
  DiamondBorderColor #4B5563
  DiamondBackgroundColor #F8FAFC
  DiamondFontColor #111827
}

start
:Enumerate the owned process group,
previously tracked identities,
and public parent-child edges;
:Inspect each relevant PID:
proc_pid_rusage, proc_pidinfo,
proc_pid_rusage again (start-token reuse check);

while (next observation?) is (yes)
  if (identity validated and live?) then (yes)
    if (still in the owned group?) then (yes)
      :Owned member:
      footprint enters the sum; <<#DBEAFE>>
    else (no: setsid, left the group)
      :Escape evidence for the whole run.
      Excluded from the sum,
      and the aggregate is not made partial; <<#F3F4F6>>
    endif
  else (no)
    if (confirmed disappearance?) then (yes)
      :Recorded as an event.
      Sum unaffected; <<#F3F4F6>>
    else (no)
      :Typed failure: stale, denied, malformed,
      unsupported, or enumeration failure.
      Aggregate becomes incomplete.
      PID and failure kind retained; <<#FEF3C7>>
    endif
  endif
endwhile (no more)

:Aggregate over owned members
(overflow is its own typed result);

if (complete and no overflow,
clock did not move backwards,
positive window duration,
within the maximum window,
within the freshness limit?) then (all hold)
  :Numeric aggregate to policy.
  A threshold comparison is allowed; <<#DCFCE7>>
else (any fails)
  :Diagnostics only.
  Known bytes and missing identities kept,
  no threshold decision from this window; <<#FEE2E2>>
endif
stop

@enduml
